From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi-i2s: program the audio interface in
 prepare

Whether a stream is non-linear PCM, and so needs NLPCM or HBR, comes
from the channel status the application writes to the "IEC958 Playback
Default" control. alsa-lib's hdmi and iec958 device definitions write
it from a hook that runs after the driver's hw_params, so the controller
was always set up for linear PCM and compressed streams were sent as
audio. hdmi-codec reads the control again for prepare, so set the
controller up there, as vc4 does.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-i2s-audio.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-i2s-audio.c
@@ -35,9 +35,9 @@
 	return audio->read(hdmi, offset);
 }
 
-static int dw_hdmi_i2s_hw_params(struct device *dev, void *data,
-				 struct hdmi_codec_daifmt *fmt,
-				 struct hdmi_codec_params *hparms)
+static int dw_hdmi_i2s_prepare(struct device *dev, void *data,
+			       struct hdmi_codec_daifmt *fmt,
+			       struct hdmi_codec_params *hparms)
 {
 	struct dw_hdmi_i2s_audio_data *audio = data;
 	struct dw_hdmi *hdmi = audio->hdmi;
@@ -207,7 +207,7 @@
 }
 
 static const struct hdmi_codec_ops dw_hdmi_i2s_ops = {
-	.hw_params	= dw_hdmi_i2s_hw_params,
+	.prepare	= dw_hdmi_i2s_prepare,
 	.audio_startup  = dw_hdmi_i2s_audio_startup,
 	.audio_shutdown	= dw_hdmi_i2s_audio_shutdown,
 	.get_eld	= dw_hdmi_i2s_get_eld,
